{"name":"Bonne Nuit","hex":"#3a4866","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bonne","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A French nursemaid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonne"}],"entries":[{"title":"Laurence BonJour","blocks":[{"text":"Laurence BonJour is an American philosopher and emeritus of Philosophy at the University of Washington."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurence_BonJour"},{"title":"Martín Bonjour","blocks":[{"text":"Martín Bonjour is an Argentine former professional footballer who played as a centre-back."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/e/ef/Mart%C3%ADn_Bonjour%2C_2012.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mart%C3%ADn_Bonjour"},{"title":"Bonne Nuit (Jersey)","blocks":[{"text":"Bonne Nuit is a small natural harbour in the Vingtaine du Nord, Saint John, Jersey, Channel Islands. Both Bonne Nuit in French and Bouonne Niet in Jèrriais mean \"good night\", referring to the shelter sailors could rely on by overnighting in the harbour. The bay nestles between the headlands of Frémont in the West and La Crête in the East."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/JY012_bba.jpg/330px-JY012_bba.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonne_Nuit_(Jersey)"},{"title":"Nuit","blocks":[{"text":"Nuit is a goddess in Thelema, a Western esoteric quasi-religion. Nuit is the speaker in the first chapter of The Book of the Law, the sacred text written or received in 1904 by Aleister Crowley. Nuit is based on the Ancient Egyptian sky goddess Nut, who in Egyptian mythology arches over her brother/husband, Geb. She is usually depicted as a naked woman who is covered with stars."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuit"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Bouonne_Niet_S